  "body": "### What is the issue with the Quirks Mode Standard?\n\nhttps://quirks.spec.whatwg.org/#the-percentage-height-calculation-quirk\n\n> In [quirks mode](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks), **for the purpose of calculating the [height](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-3/#propdef-height)** of an element element\n\nI understand this means that the modification of the containing block doesn't affect the resolution of `top: 100%` on a relpos, right?\n\nSo Firefox is wrong here:\n\n```html\n<div style=\"height: 50px; width: 50px\">\n  <div style=\"background: red\">\n    <div style=\"position: relative; height: 100%; top: 100%; background: green\"></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n| Firefox | Chrome<br>WebKit |\n| - | - |\n| <img width=\"57\" height=\"110\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d189845a-92aa-4688-afc1-a881438dc520\" /> | <img width=\"57\" height=\"110\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27c1e9fe-52fc-42de-b458-85f691e75ec0\" /> |",
